            <ArticleTitle>[The evaluation of the acute recoil of the Palmaz-Schatz stent using echography. A case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intravascular ultrasound, performed using a 0.018 in guide wire with a 30 MHz ultrasound transducer, allows to study the acute recoil of Palmaz-Schatz stent. This case showed that the acute recoil of the Palmaz-Schatz stent occurs immediately after stent implantation. The analysis of diameter and lumen cross-sectional area at the stent site was performed at different levels of dilatation. A 20% reduction of cross-sectional area was found immediately after stent expansion and balloon deflation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
